haproxy-quictls (3.4.4-2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Build without PCRE2 JIT: it needs writable+executable pages, which the
    unit's MemoryDenyWriteExecute= forbids, so haproxy rejected every regex
    in the config ("jit compilation failed") and failed to start.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:31:42 +0200

haproxy-quictls (3.4.4-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * HAProxy 3.4.4.
  * Backport OpenSSL "Fix false success on zero BIO write" into QuicTLS
    (openssl/openssl#31009): a client aborting a connection mid-response
    left record data pending and the next write hit an ossl_assert(),
    killing the worker (SIGABRT, tls_common.c:1867).
  * Build QuicTLS with CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release so ossl_assert() failures
    become connection errors instead of aborting the process.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 19:18:31 +0200

haproxy-quictls (3.4.3-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * HAProxy 3.4.3, QuicTLS 3ce7442935.
  * Switch to PCRE2 and the system Lua 5.4; drop libsystemd (HAProxy 3.x
    carries its own sd_notify).
  * Fix debian/copyright DEP-5 license paragraphs.
  * Rebuild as a dh-based source package.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 23:41:01 +0200
